2026-10-12T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2311) 'serving bonsai 2 with ninfer-all and dflash2
 # uuid: b8ca2494-f97b-5b1e-b0eb-82d6ac3a34fa
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Committed  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-10-12T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2311) 'each card serves Ternary Bonsai 2 27B through ninfer-all with a DFlash2 drafter of five tokens, and this RFD is how to set that up again from nothing on any Fedora 44 host
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2311) 'the ninfer-all fork (repository interactor-language-ninfer), the t2 `.ninfer` artifact, one systemd unit per card on Fedora 44 (native or WSL2), the mTLS front and the client's single router port
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Each card serves Bonsai 2 through ninfer-all with a DFlash2 drafter, set up from nothing.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2311) 'No RFD decided how a card serves Bonsai 2, and the setup lived in agents' notes, tied to whichever machine held the cards that week.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Build the engine and the host as the sections below say, then run the witnesses.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2311) 'serving bonsai 2 with ninfer-all and dflash2
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2311) 'A Bonsai 2 language server is ninfer-all serving the t2 `bonsai2-27b-heretic.ninfer` artifact with `--spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 5`, one server per card, each a systemd unit on Fedora 44, native or in WSL2. Each server binds loopback only and takes an API key. stunnel with mutual TLS is the only way in from off the host. Clients reach every server through one router port. Fedora 44 is the only supported OS (operator, 2026-10-17).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2311) '- RFD66606-2308 (Mac ninfer port), which uses this server as its reference.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2311) '- RFD66606-2319 (endpoint certificates), where the front's certificate comes from.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2311) '- RFD66606-2310 (eye-landmark scorer), which calls this server.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2311) 'The choice
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2311) 'The operator chose the engine and drafter on 2026-10-12 ("The ninfer with dflash won") after the A-B-A run in the details.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Blocklist
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2311) '- BLOCKLIST.md, "Speculative decoders other than MTP-3" and "1-bit PTQ1_0 bodies", both for the ggml language server.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Sources
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Drafted on 2026-10-12 from an A-B-A run on one RTX 4090. Rewritten on 2026-10-17 to describe the setup rather than the machines it ran on, after the operator unshipped the fork's Windows support and kept Fedora 44, native or WSL2.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2311) 'The measurement
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2311) 'One RTX 4090, the same launcher flags on every arm (`--max-context 262144`, `--kv-dtype rk8v4`, `--vision`, one request at a time), three repetitions, temperature 0, 512 generated tokens, speeds read from the server's own `timings`. Arms ran A-B-A so the repeated arm shows drift. Decode in tokens per second:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2311) '| Arm | chat | code | story |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2311) '| --- | --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2311) '| ninfer-all, DFlash2 K=5 | 218-232 | 314-360 | 176-187 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2311) '| prebuilt engine, MTP-3 | 206-226 | 279-282 | 176-184 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2311) '| ninfer-all, MTP-3 | 193-206 | 239-267 | 164-172 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2311) '- Prefill on ninfer-all is about 10% faster at 3k prompt tokens.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2311) '- Story is a tie inside the spread. ninfer-all with MTP-3 is the slowest arm, so the gain needs both the engine and the drafter.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2311) '- Temperature-0 text differs between the two engines and between the two drafters inside ninfer-all.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2311) '- The prebuilt engine cannot run DFlash2 on this artifact without `--lm-head-draft`, and with it DFlash2 was slower than its MTP-3 on every workload.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2311) 'The artifact
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2311) '`bonsai2-27b-heretic.ninfer`, format `t2_g128_fp16`, with the vision tower, the MTP head and the DFlash2 head inside it. The converter is pure Python and runs on the CPU, with recipe `bonsai2_27b_ternary` from the Heretic PQ2_0 body and the Bonsai-trained MTP and DFlash2 heads. The four sources and the artifact are published in the public dataset `chibifire/ninfer-bonsai2-heretic` (operator, 2026-10-12), with a sha256 to check a download against.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Every input is Apache-2.0: Qwen3.8-27B, Ternary Bonsai 2 27B, the Heretic v2 modification, the MTP and DFlash2 heads and the weights they adapt. The dataset carries their licence and notice files, a root `NOTICE` that names each author and states the conversion, and an Apache-2.0 card.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2311) 'A published artifact names no host path. A workflow in the fork converts on a clean runner and fails on any of the runner's directories in the artifact or its report, after a planted path is caught.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2311) 'The prebuilt engine reads only `t5_g128_fp16`, and ninfer-all reads only `t2_g128_fp16`. An artifact from one family does not load in the other. The artifact cannot take `--lm-head-q6`; with it the server exits at startup.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Building the engine
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2311) '`v-sekai/build.nu` in the fork builds on Fedora 44, native or WSL2, inside the fork's pixi `build` environment, which carries the compilers, CUDA, git, strip and gh. The host needs only curl to fetch pixi; git runs through `pixi exec`. The output is `dist/linux` (the programs and their library closure) and `dist/tools-linux/ninfer-install`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2311) '- One build compiles for one CUDA architecture; CMake refuses a list.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2311) '- An sm_86 build runs on an RTX 3090 and an RTX 4090, so one build serves both cards of a two-card host.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2311) '- In WSL2 the build drops the Windows entries from `PATH`, because CMake's package search over the 9p bridge takes minutes per lookup.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2311) 'The host layout
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2311) '- `/opt/ninfer/bin` and `/opt/ninfer/lib` come from `dist/linux` and are checked against its `SHA256SUMS`. `/opt/ninfer/models` holds the artifact, checked against the dataset's sha256.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2311) '- A system user `ninference` runs the servers. The key is `NINFER_API_KEY=` in `/etc/ninfer/env`, root-only, read by systemd.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2311) '- One unit per card, `ninfer-serve-<card>.service`, enabled, restarting on any exit. It sets `CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID` and picks the card with `--device`, adds `/opt/ninfer/lib` to the library path (and `/usr/lib/wsl/lib` in WSL2), and runs:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2311) '      ninfer-serve /opt/ninfer/models/bonsai2-27b-heretic.ninfer
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2311) '        --device <n> --host 127.0.0.1 --port <port> --api-key ${NINFER_API_KEY}
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2311) '        --model-id bonsai-27b --max-context 262144 --kv-capacity 262144
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2311) '        --kv-dtype rk8v4 --vision --max-concurrency 1
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2311) '        --spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 5 --no-thinking
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2311) '- The binary takes the key only on its command line, so a shell on the host sees it in `/proc`, `ps` and `systemctl status`. Mask `--api-key` whenever processes or units are listed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2311) '- In WSL2 the distribution stops when no Windows process holds it, and its units stop with it. A logon task keeps one process running in it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Reaching it
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2311) 'stunnel accepts on the host's tailnet address, one port per card, and forwards to the server's loopback port. It requires a client certificate under the chibifire Root and agent CA, and checks the client's host name against an allowlist. Its own certificate comes from RFD66606-2319. In WSL2 the tailnet address belongs to Windows, so stunnel runs there and forwards to the loopback port that WSL2 forwards into the distribution.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2311) 'On the client, a stunnel client maps each server to a local port, and a LiteLLM proxy (`v-sekai/router/` in the fork) puts all of them behind one port and one key. Its `bonsai` model goes to the least busy live server and skips one that is down; a name per card selects one server. Hermes calls only the router.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Witnesses
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Each one carries a control that must fail.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2311) '- **Ready.** `GET /v1/models` through the tunnel returns 200 with the key, and 401 without a key and with a wrong one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2311) '- **Spec.** The unit's command line, key masked, carries `--spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 5`, and the server log reports draft acceptance above zero.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2311) '- **Vision.** `v-sekai/vision_zero_shot_probe.py` against the tunnel names the red circle, the blue square and the text 42. A text-only server returns an error on the same request.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2311) '- **mTLS.** The allowlisted client gets an HTTP answer. No certificate, and a certificate for a second client under the same CA, are both refused, the second with a subject-check failure.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2311) '- **Answer.** The same temperature-0 code prompt gives the same answer hash on a rerun and after a reinstall on the same card.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2311) '- **Speed.** Three reps of a 512-token code answer at temperature 0 land inside the card's previous runs. A number without that baseline is not reported.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Pitfalls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2311) '- Check that the files the running server holds still exist before a restart. A server keeps serving from a deleted model file, and the restart then fails with `startup failed | inspecting artifact`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2311) '- `CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID` changes which card a device index names. Read `nvidia-smi` in the same order before choosing `--device`; a build for a newer architecture fails on an older card with `no kernel image`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2311) '- Wait for the ready line `listening on` with a journal cursor taken before the restart, not with a timestamp.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2311) '- An A/B that swaps `--spec` restores the unit in the same script on failure, because a server that dies at startup leaves its card down.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Open questions
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2311) '- The decider benchmark behind the MTP-3 blocklist row has not been run on ninfer-all. Until it is, the row and this RFD measure different workloads, and neither says which drafter makes better decisions.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2311) '- MTP's upstream advantage is a second request lane (`--max-concurrency 2`). Every arm here served one request at a time.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2311) '- DFlash2 at six and seven draft tokens is measured on one card only.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2311) '- The unit and stunnel files are written by hand on each host and are in no repository.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2311) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-12T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2311) 'Every move of the cards rebuilt it by hand.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2311  1 LINE
 Text:Written
